      "mergeID": "62d1a556e0d427519debc09c",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Documents folder is not a great place for configuration files that are not meant for users to see/delete/etc.  The better place for this is the appdata folder.\n\nEDIT: In response to the findability of the json file, it's literally linked directly in the settings page.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[FEEDBACK, 0.2.0] Change default configuration directory to appdata instead of documents.",
      "parentID": "628d228cb624bb0b623b14da",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "628422e5905abe0b7107aa61",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name}: settings.json and others (Documents\\VRChatCreatorCompanion) are not user's documents. Probably you don't want users to directly touch them. In general, apps' own preferences and data should be located at %APPDATA% (%USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Roaming), one of Windows' known folders.\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/shell/knownfolderid\nSome frameworks support this folder to store application data. For example, Electron's `app.getPath('userData')` method returns %APPDATA%\\Foo and VSCode which uses Electron is actually using %APPDATA%\\Code to store data.\nhttps://www.electronjs.org/docs/latest/api/app#appgetpathname",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "62a3ac301d989b0ba5e3db4d",
      "author": {
