      ],
      "mergeID": "62d1a556e0d427519debc09c",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Documents folder is not a great place for configuration files that are not meant for users to see/delete/etc.  The better place for this is the appdata folder.\n\nEDIT: In response to the findability of the json file, it's literally linked directly in the settings page.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[FEEDBACK, 0.2.0] Change default configuration directory to appdata instead of documents.",
      "parentID": "628d228cb624bb0b623b14da",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "628422e5905abe0b7107aa61",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5deb0e4d299b3347978ea6a2|full_name}: Users are more than welcome to manually modify their settings file, and the \"Templates\" folder is 100% user documents. We are considering moving the location of these items from Documents to AppData, and if you feel strongly about it, it would help make the case if you could speak to why this is an issue. For example, if you have experienced or know of permissions issues with reading and writing from the Documents folder vs an AppData folder.\nI think it's worth noting that many applications store information here, including Visual Studio, Steam, Ableton Live, every Rockstar Game, etc. If this is simply a matter of opinion, that's fine - but no one has yet brought up an actual issue caused by this location, which makes this a very low-priority item compared to active bugs, etc.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "62a58e974d2de00bb3729918",
      "author": {
